WEBVTT

00:21.309 --> 00:22.779
(Ryeo Un)

00:24.049 --> 00:25.920
(Choi Hyun Wook)

00:27.990 --> 00:29.650
(Seol In Ah)

00:34.689 --> 00:36.630
(Shin Eun Soo)

00:44.240 --> 00:48.008
(Twinkling Watermelon)

00:48.009 --> 00:49.239
(Production sponsors)

00:49.240 --> 00:50.739
(Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism, KOCCA)

00:50.740 --> 00:51.740
(All people, organizations, locations, and incidents...)

00:51.740 --> 00:52.740
(in this drama are fictitious.)

00:52.740 --> 00:53.740
(Staff ensured child actors' safety in the filming of this drama.)

00:54.880 --> 00:57.920
"Sorry. I shouldn't have let myself fall for you. I made a mistake."

00:59.350 --> 01:01.550
"I have a dream and goals."

01:01.789 --> 01:04.759
"It's my dream and my family's dream too."

01:05.719 --> 01:07.219
"At this stage of my life, dating someone..."

01:07.319 --> 01:10.560
"would feel like a waste of emotion and time, which is useless."

01:11.560 --> 01:13.660
"Useless?" What?

01:14.060 --> 01:15.999
That's what Eun Ho wanted me to tell you.

01:20.869 --> 01:22.209
Tell me yourself.

01:22.640 --> 01:24.280
I don't believe this guy.

01:24.880 --> 01:27.239
(Tell me yourself. I don't believe this guy.)

01:27.240 --> 01:28.709
I'll DM you later.

01:31.880 --> 01:33.948
Sorry. Don't contact him until he gets into college...

01:33.949 --> 01:36.289
- Hey!
- He asked me to tell you that.

01:50.470 --> 01:51.800
You selfish jerk.

01:58.140 --> 01:59.209
Shut it.

02:00.780 --> 02:03.080
(Episode 10)

02:11.890 --> 02:14.459
Four down. There's just one left now, right?

02:15.059 --> 02:16.229
Hand over her number now.

02:17.160 --> 02:19.229
No way. This one, I really can't.

02:19.399 --> 02:21.129
"No way?" What do you mean?

02:21.130 --> 02:23.870
You promised me you'd cut off contact with all of them.

02:25.199 --> 02:26.970
Hurry up and hand it over.

02:27.100 --> 02:28.639
It's that cellist girl, right?

02:28.769 --> 02:30.310
Hand it over. Come on.

02:32.680 --> 02:35.150
No, she's special to me.

02:38.680 --> 02:41.590
This is such a critical time for you. Don't you know that?

02:43.389 --> 02:44.589
Getting into college won't be easy...

02:44.590 --> 02:46.720
even if you're focused solely on the training.

02:47.560 --> 02:49.889
You need to start seriously thinking about your future.

02:50.829 --> 02:53.299
You're doing this for your own future, not mine.

02:53.900 --> 02:54.970
What?

02:55.130 --> 02:57.900
I need to achieve my dream for you to free yourself from this burden.

02:58.900 --> 02:59.940
Eun Ho.

03:03.269 --> 03:06.780
Eun Gyeol, just live your life.

03:06.979 --> 03:09.049
I'll figure out what to do with my own life.

03:12.919 --> 03:15.720
From time to time, let yourself enjoy the moment.

03:16.549 --> 03:18.660
Let yourself fall in love, like me.

03:19.460 --> 03:21.858
Don't waste your youth because of me or the family...

03:21.859 --> 03:24.229
because you can never get back your youth.

03:24.930 --> 03:26.729
Let yourself twinkle while you can.

03:27.699 --> 03:29.600
Do things that make your heart flutter.

03:30.299 --> 03:32.440
It won't make your world come crashing down.

04:01.530 --> 04:02.729
You've grown up to be a fine young man.

04:03.930 --> 04:06.539
Do you want to come in for a moment? I have something to give you.

04:12.910 --> 04:15.850
My gosh. Abstinence can be charming.

04:16.850 --> 04:18.150
Your self-restraint is impressive.

04:20.479 --> 04:21.889
I must be going crazy.

04:22.049 --> 04:23.488
Ms. Choi gave me Mr. Viva's guitar.

04:23.489 --> 04:25.489
I should thank her if anything. What was I doing, just now?

04:27.160 --> 04:30.289
Come on. It's okay.

04:30.789 --> 04:32.829
The embarrassment will keep you up at night for a month.

04:32.830 --> 04:34.199
But after that, you'll forget it in no time.

04:34.200 --> 04:35.669
Embarrassing memories are precious too, you see.

04:38.539 --> 04:41.809
My gosh. It's okay.

04:42.039 --> 04:43.569
Having a crush on someone is a valuable experience too,

04:43.570 --> 04:44.910
like your first love.

04:45.640 --> 04:47.809
And be honoured that I'm your crush.

04:49.150 --> 04:52.179
Do you remember, Eun Ho? That day, you told me...

04:52.749 --> 04:56.549
that life didn't have to be perfect for it to shine.

04:56.890 --> 04:58.820
It's the little moments that make your life twinkle,

04:59.260 --> 05:00.390
and happiness is...

05:00.590 --> 05:03.229
what you experience when those moments come together.

05:04.729 --> 05:07.129
But be honest with me.

05:07.359 --> 05:09.270
Can I really let myself twinkle from time to time?

05:09.470 --> 05:10.668
I bet you've never dated.

05:10.669 --> 05:12.999
Can I let myself follow my heart from time to time?

05:13.270 --> 05:15.369
You've never dated, right? I knew it!

05:15.910 --> 05:17.609
Would my world really not come crashing down?

05:18.210 --> 05:21.280
Look at you, you've never dated

05:21.450 --> 05:22.879
You've never dated

06:06.059 --> 06:07.059
Hey.

06:08.429 --> 06:09.530
Well...

06:11.330 --> 06:12.330
That portrait.

06:14.229 --> 06:15.970
Is that me?

06:26.080 --> 06:27.080
But why?

06:29.910 --> 06:30.950
Don't tell me...

06:33.280 --> 06:34.890
Hey, do you...

06:38.960 --> 06:39.960
like me?

07:12.090 --> 07:13.489
- Hey, you know...
- Hey.

07:15.689 --> 07:16.789
- You go first.
- You go first.

07:18.760 --> 07:20.200
- Or shall I...
- Shall I go first?

07:24.570 --> 07:26.640
- About earlier...
- Let's pretend it never happened.

07:28.210 --> 07:30.340
Yes, I get it.

07:30.669 --> 07:33.609
This weather, the moist air, and this romantic ambience.

07:33.939 --> 07:35.548
All these things...

07:35.549 --> 07:37.950
provoked your dirty mind.

07:39.220 --> 07:41.080
"Dirty mind?" What?

07:42.419 --> 07:44.150
It's okay. I really understand.

07:44.590 --> 07:46.918
Well, let's just pretend it never happened...

07:46.919 --> 07:48.890
and keep some distance from each other.

07:52.760 --> 07:54.830
Always stay at least 5m away from me, okay?

07:56.530 --> 07:57.869
Why should I do that?

07:58.369 --> 07:59.640
You know why.

07:59.840 --> 08:02.709
You cheated to steal the ball from Yi Chan.

08:02.710 --> 08:05.709
Like I said, I want to be fair to you both until the festival...

08:05.710 --> 08:07.309
You're not entirely wrong,

08:08.210 --> 08:09.609
but you're building up walls around you.

08:11.010 --> 08:12.619
I'm a little offended.

08:13.950 --> 08:15.419
Of course, I...

08:16.390 --> 08:18.260
I can't say I'm not partially responsible.

08:18.660 --> 08:21.728
Gosh, boys at age 18 are like beasts.

08:21.729 --> 08:23.929
I admit that I let my guard down.

08:24.189 --> 08:26.429
Then I'll knock 2m off.

08:26.530 --> 08:28.400
Always stay at least 3m away from me, okay?

08:32.799 --> 08:34.770
- About what happened earlier...
- Okay, fine.

08:34.939 --> 08:37.710
Always stay at least 2m away from me. End of discussion.

08:37.979 --> 08:39.010
Bye.

08:58.460 --> 09:01.259
This is nuts. I must be losing my mind!

09:01.430 --> 09:04.069
"About what happened earlier?" What were you going to say?

09:04.070 --> 09:05.799
That you're sorry? That it was a mistake?

09:05.800 --> 09:08.170
That it was part of your mission or something? If not that...

09:21.180 --> 09:22.290
If not that,

09:25.060 --> 09:26.259
what was it?

09:28.759 --> 09:29.859
What happened earlier.

09:41.540 --> 09:42.540
What's up?

09:43.040 --> 09:45.180
What is it? Where are we going?

10:00.889 --> 10:03.029
What do those signs mean?

10:03.629 --> 10:05.499
(What do those signs mean?)

10:07.659 --> 10:10.830
It means, "Don't go. Stay with me."

10:14.070 --> 10:15.970
Why do you ask? Did someone say that to you?

10:18.909 --> 10:19.979
Then what about this?

10:21.749 --> 10:25.519
"Thank you for saving me."

10:26.249 --> 10:28.619
"And I'm sorry."

10:29.420 --> 10:32.489
"I didn't know that you were the one who saved me."

10:33.420 --> 10:34.619
It was Yi Chan, wasn't it?

10:38.060 --> 10:39.960
Yi Chan said that. Am I right?

10:43.600 --> 10:44.840
It's a green light.

10:47.139 --> 10:48.970
I want to learn sign language.

10:51.210 --> 10:52.979
So I can make friends.

10:53.580 --> 10:55.108
You'll teach me, right?

10:55.109 --> 10:56.749
(You'll teach me, right?)

11:02.950 --> 11:05.759
Yes. I'll teach you.

11:06.519 --> 11:08.060
I'll do my very best.

11:25.580 --> 11:28.509
So it's been a few days. Are you enjoying working as a live-in tutor?

11:28.749 --> 11:30.050
Yes, it's been good.

11:30.249 --> 11:32.149
You remember the promise you made me, right?

11:33.279 --> 11:36.089
Let me say it again. I'll have to see results in a month.

11:36.090 --> 11:37.420
If not, there will be consequences.

11:37.820 --> 11:40.889
Please don't worry. I always keep my promises.

11:41.629 --> 11:42.830
I'll look forward to it, then.

11:43.560 --> 11:45.430
- You can go.
- Yes, sir.

11:52.470 --> 11:54.070
Do you have something else to say?

11:55.570 --> 11:58.278
Sir, you have a business trip coming up.

11:58.279 --> 12:00.639
Why don't you bring back a fax machine as a gift for your daughter?

12:03.350 --> 12:06.580
I saved you, and you're now telling me what to do?

12:07.350 --> 12:09.648
If you buy her a fax machine as a gift,

12:09.649 --> 12:11.690
she can use it to communicate with the world.

12:12.320 --> 12:14.960
It could also help you achieve the results you want more quickly.

12:15.090 --> 12:18.129
I suppose you haven't learned what it means to overstep boundaries.

12:18.529 --> 12:21.499
I just meant that it could maximize your gains, which is what you like.

12:22.070 --> 12:23.129
All right, then.

12:29.170 --> 12:31.540
Why should I accept your request?

12:32.340 --> 12:34.540
I'm a businessman. I never take on deals that could result in losses.

12:35.180 --> 12:37.909
When I give 1 thing, I always gain at least 2 things.

12:38.550 --> 12:41.550
What could you offer if I were to accept your request?

12:42.050 --> 12:43.420
What could you give me?

12:54.430 --> 12:55.769
Her smile.

12:56.769 --> 12:57.769
What?

12:59.139 --> 13:01.399
I'll show you your daughter's smile.

13:01.940 --> 13:03.340
Not a fake one.

13:03.739 --> 13:06.340
A real smile. The kind you can only see when someone's truly happy.

13:45.149 --> 13:46.149
What?

13:52.460 --> 13:54.820
I'm leaving this here as I must stay at least 2m away from you.

13:55.259 --> 13:57.228
I washed it for you while filling up gas...

13:57.229 --> 13:58.659
and fixed a few things too.

14:00.430 --> 14:01.899
Of course, he has to tell me he did these things.

14:02.369 --> 14:04.498
Today's temperature, humidity level, ambience,

14:04.499 --> 14:07.700
and the whole universe wish you a wonderful day.

14:18.379 --> 14:19.779
Do you want to practice?

14:21.519 --> 14:24.989
"I want to be your friend."

14:27.420 --> 14:31.190
"I want to get to know you better."

14:33.060 --> 14:34.159
Well done.

14:51.820 --> 14:54.220
It's very nice to see the two of you on your way to school together.

14:55.619 --> 14:58.320
Can you spare me a moment before your class?

14:58.920 --> 15:01.960
(Seowon Arts High School)

15:09.769 --> 15:10.830
Eun Gyeol.

15:12.269 --> 15:13.300
Yes, ma'am.

15:14.300 --> 15:15.440
Am I a joke to you?

15:16.540 --> 15:17.570
Pardon me?

15:17.840 --> 15:19.878
I clearly told you that you weren't allowed...

15:19.879 --> 15:21.210
to use sign language in my house.

15:21.710 --> 15:23.950
I'd like to know your reason, one that I can understand.

15:26.220 --> 15:28.749
The family has its own education method.

15:29.790 --> 15:31.789
I can confidently say that it is the best way to raise Chung Ah...

15:31.790 --> 15:33.290
like a non-deaf person.

15:34.290 --> 15:35.859
Are you sure that is the only reason?

15:36.190 --> 15:37.529
What other reason could there be?

15:39.259 --> 15:41.560
Perhaps, you're deliberately isolating Chung Ah...

15:41.999 --> 15:44.499
and trying to make sure she can't communicate with Chairman Yoon...

15:45.170 --> 15:46.340
to get something.

15:49.570 --> 15:51.310
Jinsung Musical Instruments, for example.

16:00.279 --> 16:02.790
You seem to think that you're holding on to a sturdy rope.

16:03.690 --> 16:04.790
But you see...

16:05.889 --> 16:09.330
How many days out of the year do you think the chairman comes home?

16:09.989 --> 16:11.930
So when he's not around to see what's going on,

16:15.600 --> 16:18.070
you've been abusing Chung Ah in places he can't see?

16:18.739 --> 16:19.840
How dare you!

16:20.470 --> 16:22.269
That statement is considered slander.

16:24.509 --> 16:26.279
If I abused Chung Ah,

16:26.609 --> 16:28.979
how come the chairman has never once heard about it?

16:29.649 --> 16:32.619
There are many eyes and mouths in the household.

16:35.019 --> 16:38.388
All our employees believe in my education philosophy and obey...

16:38.389 --> 16:40.259
They keep their lips sealed because you pay them.

16:45.430 --> 16:47.330
I have that much insight.

16:49.129 --> 16:51.670
If you're thinking of suggesting the same thing to me,

16:52.840 --> 16:54.070
I must decline.

16:55.710 --> 16:57.239
If you have nothing else to say...

16:57.310 --> 16:58.680
The Guidance Committee...

16:59.479 --> 17:01.509
has decided to take the disciplinary action up a notch.

17:02.810 --> 17:05.050
You'll have to clean the school for a month...

17:05.350 --> 17:06.979
instead of attending your classes.

17:07.479 --> 17:09.619
But I was already told to submit letters of apology and volunteer...

17:14.759 --> 17:16.430
Are you doing this to get back at me?

17:18.060 --> 17:19.959
So I can't help Chung Ah study?

17:26.699 --> 17:29.740
Have you heard the idiom about the fox using the tiger's power?

17:39.149 --> 17:40.179
Darn it.

17:43.719 --> 17:46.790
The fox acted up, believing that the tiger had its back.

17:49.429 --> 17:50.590
What happened to the fox in the end?

17:51.560 --> 17:52.899
It survived,

17:53.830 --> 17:55.159
and it was not foolish.

17:56.830 --> 17:59.169
I believe the contract you signed with the chairman is for a month.

17:59.770 --> 18:01.600
You'd better leave before that.

18:03.469 --> 18:06.509
I'm sorry, but Chairman Yoon is my employer, not you.

18:06.510 --> 18:07.580
Leave.

18:11.080 --> 18:13.379
Move out of my house and leave my school.

18:13.980 --> 18:15.989
I don't care who you really are and what you're truly after.

18:15.990 --> 18:17.520
Go back to where you came from.

18:19.590 --> 18:20.689
Mark my words.

18:22.490 --> 18:23.959
If you ignore my warning,

18:24.590 --> 18:26.299
you'll witness the miserable demise...

18:26.300 --> 18:28.629
of the arrogant fox firsthand.

18:34.000 --> 18:36.169
Gosh, this really is nuts.

18:36.810 --> 18:39.609
I can't leave until my job here is done.

18:39.879 --> 18:42.049
Besides, I need to know how I can go back...

18:42.050 --> 18:44.449
to decide whether or not to go back.

18:45.379 --> 18:46.879
Darn it.

19:01.500 --> 19:02.570
What is this?

19:48.139 --> 19:50.249
- Hello?
- Good day!

19:50.250 --> 19:51.579
You've got to be kidding me!

19:51.580 --> 19:54.480
Goodness. How scary. Are you a tiger or something?

19:54.879 --> 19:57.589
Gosh. Why are you so angry today?

19:57.590 --> 19:59.290
How could I not be angry?

19:59.520 --> 20:01.118
You call me whenever you want...

20:01.119 --> 20:02.529
and always hang up on me.

20:02.530 --> 20:04.458
I can't even reach you when I need you.

20:04.459 --> 20:07.358
All right, calm down. Let's talk it out.

20:07.359 --> 20:08.530
"Talk it out?" As if!

20:09.030 --> 20:11.399
You'll just say things that sound like riddles anyway.

20:11.500 --> 20:12.898
You never once answered my questions...

20:12.899 --> 20:14.740
or did me a favour.

20:14.969 --> 20:17.968
Oh, no. I guess you needed my help.

20:17.969 --> 20:20.310
If I did, so what?

20:20.510 --> 20:21.779
It's not like you'd help me.

20:21.780 --> 20:24.279
I'm not such a terrible person, you see.

20:24.280 --> 20:25.619
My goodness.

20:28.350 --> 20:30.449
Then please tell me when my dad's accident took place.

20:31.149 --> 20:33.388
You're still obsessed with the problems involving your parents.

20:33.389 --> 20:35.830
When and where did the accident take place? And why did it happen?

20:36.590 --> 20:39.699
Can't you stop obsessing over it and start enjoying your youth?

20:43.469 --> 20:45.230
Do not contact me again.

20:46.699 --> 20:47.770
I'm just going to...

20:48.040 --> 20:49.869
figure out what to do on my own.

20:50.409 --> 20:51.469
Too bad.

20:51.570 --> 20:53.708
Actually, I found and sent...

20:53.709 --> 20:56.050
the perfect helper for you.

20:56.280 --> 20:58.279
But you want to figure things out on your own,

20:58.280 --> 20:59.618
so you do that. Bye.

20:59.619 --> 21:01.619
No, hold on. Wait!

21:02.389 --> 21:04.550
"Helper?" Who's that?

21:04.750 --> 21:05.959
Go softer.

21:10.760 --> 21:12.230
Gradually increase the volume.

21:32.980 --> 21:35.590
For some strange reason, they seem to have good chemistry.

21:35.990 --> 21:37.850
They resemble each other in some peculiar ways.

21:39.159 --> 21:40.959
They say people look alike when they're in love.

21:55.540 --> 21:56.570
Se Gyeong.

21:57.469 --> 21:58.510
Choi Se Gyeong?

22:01.480 --> 22:02.510
Choi Se Gyeong.

22:03.449 --> 22:04.509
Yes?

22:04.510 --> 22:07.079
What were you thinking about? I called your name several times.

22:07.080 --> 22:08.148
Oh, I'm sorry.

22:08.149 --> 22:10.090
I'm still having a hard time adjusting to the time difference.

22:10.149 --> 22:12.790
Come on out and delight our ears. It's been too long.

22:13.119 --> 22:14.159
Sir.

22:14.459 --> 22:16.658
I was told to just observe the classes for the time being.

22:16.659 --> 22:17.989
That's why I didn't bring my cello.

22:17.990 --> 22:20.459
Guys, can one of you let her borrow your cello?

22:21.399 --> 22:22.469
Here.

23:03.609 --> 23:05.709
(Our Deepest Condolences)

23:08.540 --> 23:11.280
You must be devastated, but be mature about it and get over it.

23:11.409 --> 23:12.678
You don't want people to say you won...

23:12.679 --> 23:14.980
first place by default because of a friend who took her own life.

23:20.020 --> 23:22.020
Gosh, sir.

23:22.359 --> 23:24.389
Here. I'm sorry.

23:24.859 --> 23:27.429
I need to run to the restroom now.

23:27.899 --> 23:30.530
Gosh, I apologize. I'm sorry.

23:50.320 --> 23:51.719
Don't let your mind falter.

23:52.490 --> 23:53.520
But...

23:54.060 --> 23:56.129
remember these emotions you're feeling now...

23:57.590 --> 24:00.730
so you can think of them when you're playing sad music later on.

24:29.560 --> 24:30.560
What's she doing?

24:30.929 --> 24:31.990
I can't hear it.

24:32.459 --> 24:33.499
(The 47th Seokwang Music Competition)

24:33.500 --> 24:34.600
I hear no sound.

24:36.030 --> 24:37.869
I can't hear anything!

24:43.969 --> 24:45.070
Too bad.

24:45.209 --> 24:47.079
Actually, I found and sent...

24:47.080 --> 24:49.280
the perfect helper for you.

24:52.520 --> 24:53.580
"Helper?"

25:12.740 --> 25:13.770
Dad?

25:14.399 --> 25:15.500
What's going on?

25:21.709 --> 25:23.250
There's one condition.

25:26.919 --> 25:29.020
To receive help from your helper,

25:30.689 --> 25:34.060
you must help them first.

25:56.649 --> 26:02.520
Your silence

26:04.419 --> 26:09.129
Makes my lips dry

26:10.929 --> 26:15.869
The cold look in your eyes

26:20.270 --> 26:21.300
What should I do?

26:21.740 --> 26:22.810
What should I say?

26:24.169 --> 26:25.510
She'll be hurt if I reject her.

26:26.540 --> 26:28.010
But I should still be honest, right?

26:28.980 --> 26:31.280
I'm sorry, but there's someone I like...

26:35.820 --> 26:36.889
It's for me?

26:40.419 --> 26:41.790
Hey, wait. Chung Ah!

26:51.129 --> 26:54.540
I know you like Se Gyeong.

26:59.340 --> 27:00.439
It doesn't matter though,

27:01.040 --> 27:02.080
because...

27:04.980 --> 27:07.480
(You own your feelings, and I own mine.)

27:10.149 --> 27:11.949
You own your feelings,

27:15.260 --> 27:17.060
and I own mine.

27:29.340 --> 27:31.939
But we can still be friends.

27:35.609 --> 27:38.580
If you don't want to be my friend because of my disability...

27:38.750 --> 27:39.820
It's not that.

27:42.850 --> 27:44.388
Then you're a jerk.

27:44.389 --> 27:46.520
I'll just spit on you and walk away,

27:46.659 --> 27:47.889
so feel free to reject me.

27:54.359 --> 27:57.770
Can we be friends?

28:03.240 --> 28:10.780
As I was turning around

28:11.050 --> 28:17.750
Instead of telling me that you loved me

28:18.919 --> 28:20.820
You said, "Goodbye"

28:22.560 --> 28:24.359
Goodbye

28:26.959 --> 28:31.730
The one word that got me choked up

28:33.740 --> 28:39.280
Because our love

28:41.540 --> 28:47.179
Wasn't meant

28:48.280 --> 28:52.020
To last

29:13.609 --> 29:15.240
Hey, when did you improve so much?

29:15.609 --> 29:17.679
You must've been practicing really hard!

29:18.109 --> 29:20.049
My gosh. Let me check your calluses.

29:20.050 --> 29:22.618
Goodness. What took you so long?

29:22.619 --> 29:23.948
I told you to come at the speed of light.

29:23.949 --> 29:25.349
Right, you said it was urgent.

29:25.350 --> 29:26.519
Why? What happened?

29:26.520 --> 29:27.790
Are you hurt?

29:27.959 --> 29:29.059
Did you get into another fight?

29:29.060 --> 29:30.489
We have to share the results of the skills test...

29:30.490 --> 29:32.429
and make our decision!

29:32.560 --> 29:35.358
Hey! You got me so worried because you said it was an emergency.

29:35.359 --> 29:36.799
I nearly had a heart attack.

29:36.800 --> 29:38.069
Choose your words mindfully.

29:38.070 --> 29:39.240
It is an emergency!

29:39.399 --> 29:41.600
The festival is right around the corner. Anyway, forget it.

29:42.139 --> 29:45.340
So? How did the test go? I have no doubt that she passed.

29:46.179 --> 29:48.009
You got to see firsthand...

29:48.010 --> 29:50.050
how talented Se Gyeong really is.

30:00.159 --> 30:01.189
I did get to see her...

30:02.189 --> 30:03.260
up close.

30:04.530 --> 30:05.530
She looked pretty.

30:06.359 --> 30:07.359
What?

30:07.730 --> 30:09.059
You little...

30:09.060 --> 30:10.628
No, it came out wrong. The photos she took!

30:10.629 --> 30:12.840
I meant to say the photos she took were pretty.

30:13.300 --> 30:14.939
What about you?

30:15.300 --> 30:17.040
You saw Chung Ah's drawings, right?

30:29.080 --> 30:30.149
Oh...

30:35.820 --> 30:36.889
She's pretty good.

30:38.590 --> 30:39.760
I guess you do...

30:40.929 --> 30:42.260
respect the frontman after all.

30:43.730 --> 30:44.770
So can she work with us?

30:46.070 --> 30:49.438
Well, what do you say? Can Se Gyeong work with us?

30:49.439 --> 30:50.809
If Chung Ah can work with us...

30:50.810 --> 30:52.209
Yes, for sure.

30:54.679 --> 30:57.149
Nothing personal though. It's strictly business.

30:57.850 --> 30:59.719
The deal's sealed. Don't go back on your word later.

31:02.080 --> 31:03.819
All right, look here.

31:03.820 --> 31:06.388
One, two, three. Snap!

31:06.389 --> 31:07.459
You little...

31:07.619 --> 31:11.428
My. What is this, the KOREA-US summit?

31:11.429 --> 31:14.928
My gosh. I feel like a peaceful reunification is around the corner.

31:14.929 --> 31:18.029
Goodness. We don't have time to be chatting away like this.

31:18.030 --> 31:20.300
Oh, you're right. Let's get going. We'll be late.

31:20.699 --> 31:21.740
Where are we going?

31:22.300 --> 31:23.709
- All right.
- Goodness.

31:23.909 --> 31:25.169
Someone wants to see us.

31:25.770 --> 31:26.780
Who?

31:27.980 --> 31:29.709
The almighty landlord.

31:30.209 --> 31:34.580
The kind helper who is letting us use this practice room.

31:36.490 --> 31:37.520
"Helper?"

31:37.949 --> 31:39.859
(White Night)

31:40.590 --> 31:42.119
Finally, we're here.

31:42.929 --> 31:44.789
What? This place is...

31:44.790 --> 31:46.499
Hey, why are you standing there?

31:46.500 --> 31:47.760
Sorry, I'm coming.

31:48.030 --> 31:49.060
Hurry!

31:52.770 --> 31:54.539
Sir, we're here!

31:54.540 --> 31:56.339
- It's good to see you guys.
- Hello.

31:56.340 --> 31:58.469
- Yes, hi.
- Hello!

31:59.139 --> 32:00.840
- Oh.
- My gosh.

32:01.139 --> 32:03.979
It's you, right? The boy who came to buy a guitar for his dad.

32:03.980 --> 32:07.050
My gosh. I was wondering, but you actually own this building?

32:08.149 --> 32:09.749
Anyway, why didn't you come back?

32:09.750 --> 32:11.889
I had found a nice guitar for you.

32:12.090 --> 32:16.459
Oh, I had a complicated situation.

32:16.590 --> 32:19.060
Why? You couldn't reconcile with your dad?

32:19.500 --> 32:21.199
He doesn't want to start a band with you anymore?

32:21.459 --> 32:22.659
How did you know?

32:26.300 --> 32:27.399
You have a dad?

32:29.770 --> 32:31.869
Yes, I do.

32:34.040 --> 32:35.409
But he's very immature.

32:35.840 --> 32:37.909
My gosh. How rude.

32:38.909 --> 32:40.879
I bet you rebelled against him and ran away from home.

32:41.350 --> 32:44.049
Go home and behave yourself, you idiot.

32:44.050 --> 32:46.918
If you want to rebel, do it while eating home-cooked meals.

32:46.919 --> 32:49.629
Even if you want to fight, at least make sure you sleep in a warm room.

32:49.830 --> 32:51.659
Do it at home, okay?

32:52.560 --> 32:53.560
Don't you worry.

32:53.659 --> 32:55.300
I'll go back as soon as my job here is done.

32:56.730 --> 32:58.229
I'm doing my best.

32:58.230 --> 33:00.868
Yes, keep trying your best and be a good son.

33:00.869 --> 33:02.869
Sir, why did you call us here today?

33:03.469 --> 33:05.339
I can order more food for you guys, so eat up.

33:05.340 --> 33:06.780
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

33:10.179 --> 33:13.049
Hyun Yul, do you still fight with Jindo dogs?

33:13.050 --> 33:14.379
No way.

33:14.580 --> 33:16.648
These days, you can get arrested for touching the Natural Treasures.

33:16.649 --> 33:17.689
My goodness.

33:18.649 --> 33:20.919
Sir, how do you and Hyun Yul know each other?

33:21.060 --> 33:23.729
I think Hyun Yul and I met when he was...

33:23.730 --> 33:24.889
in the Hongdae indie scene.

33:25.760 --> 33:26.760
Yes.

33:27.129 --> 33:29.629
He taught the leader of my band.

33:30.600 --> 33:32.770
Really? What did he teach him?

33:33.040 --> 33:34.040
Guitar.

33:34.340 --> 33:37.009
Oh, I should've properly introduced him sooner.

33:37.010 --> 33:39.009
In his prime,

33:39.010 --> 33:40.878
he took the entire indie band scene by storm...

33:40.879 --> 33:42.739
with his guitar alone.

33:42.740 --> 33:44.079
He's like a legend.

33:44.080 --> 33:46.080
- Oh, my!
- My gosh!

33:46.179 --> 33:47.349
That's so cool.

33:47.350 --> 33:50.049
A legend? No. It's all in the past.

33:50.050 --> 33:51.119
Come on.

33:51.250 --> 33:53.590
Oh, sir. This guy here is a good guitarist.

33:54.419 --> 33:56.989
When I heard him play the guitar for the first time, I was shocked...

33:56.990 --> 33:58.629
because it sounded similar to his style.

33:58.790 --> 33:59.830
Really?

34:00.030 --> 34:01.628
Can I hear it sometime?

34:01.629 --> 34:04.429
Gosh, Hyun Yul was just exaggerating.

34:05.030 --> 34:08.040
I'd love to hear you play the guitar, sir.

34:09.240 --> 34:11.368
These days, all I can do is sand the guitars.

34:11.369 --> 34:13.709
My fingers aren't flexible anymore, so I can no longer play.

34:14.439 --> 34:16.980
Could he be the "helper" Master was talking about?

34:17.679 --> 34:20.619
If he is, what can he help me with?

34:21.520 --> 34:24.219
The practice room? Musical advice?

34:24.889 --> 34:26.960
But that's not the kind of help I want.

34:27.759 --> 34:31.029
Anyway, he should be here soon.

34:32.259 --> 34:33.330
Is someone else joining us?

34:33.529 --> 34:36.060
I want to introduce you to someone.

34:36.969 --> 34:39.229
Meet him, and he'll help you guys out...

34:39.230 --> 34:41.440
for many years to come. Consider him a helper.

34:41.600 --> 34:42.639
"Helper?"

35:01.589 --> 35:02.989
Who is the helper?

35:03.389 --> 35:04.759
You must've heard of him.

35:05.029 --> 35:07.659
The genius guitarist of the century from Chuncheon.

35:08.429 --> 35:12.330
Yoon Dong Jin.

35:16.100 --> 35:17.569
Come on in, Dong Jin.

35:18.369 --> 35:21.080
It's been a while.

35:21.540 --> 35:23.109
It's good to see you here.

35:23.110 --> 35:25.249
- Hello.
- Hello.

35:25.250 --> 35:27.278
- Come here.
- Take a seat.

35:27.279 --> 35:28.979
- You can sit here.
- You can sit here.

35:28.980 --> 35:30.650
Bring a glass for him.

35:31.219 --> 35:33.859
- Have you eaten?
- Yes, I have. Look at the time.

35:33.860 --> 35:35.619
- Just give me a glass of beer.
- All right.

35:39.029 --> 35:40.299
Your jaw might drop.

35:41.830 --> 35:44.899
Sit down. I have a turtle neck syndrome. It's hard to look up.

35:44.900 --> 35:47.069
Sit down. He said he had a turtle neck syndrome.

35:48.400 --> 35:50.009
That's cute.

35:56.009 --> 35:58.449
So you're a school band?

35:58.679 --> 35:59.778
- Yes.
- Yes.

35:59.779 --> 36:00.948
Who is the frontman?

36:00.949 --> 36:02.049
- It's him.
- It's him.

36:10.130 --> 36:11.560
Go.

36:15.000 --> 36:16.029
Hey.

36:21.469 --> 36:23.369
What was it? Why was Dong Jin there?

36:24.009 --> 36:26.210
What was it? Is Dong Jin the helper?

36:26.980 --> 36:30.080
What was it? Did we run away when the legend showed himself?

36:30.850 --> 36:32.150
It's your fault.

36:32.380 --> 36:34.048
If you hadn't lied that day,

36:34.049 --> 36:36.218
they would've not thought that we were tricksters.

36:36.219 --> 36:39.719
Wait. We can't get out of it just by hiding.

36:42.360 --> 36:43.529
Oh, gosh.

36:44.429 --> 36:45.560
Did you hear that?

36:45.659 --> 36:48.730
He said he would've taken a bath if he had known beforehand.

36:48.960 --> 36:51.069
You're loving it.

36:51.199 --> 36:53.239
- Can I hold your hand once?
- Sure.

36:53.699 --> 36:56.638
You were like a dragon in a legend,

36:56.639 --> 36:58.739
a unicorn in my imagination.

36:59.069 --> 37:02.179
Thank you so much for paying a visit.

37:03.650 --> 37:05.710
I want to be your orb.

37:06.049 --> 37:08.219
Bite me when you're bored.

37:09.119 --> 37:10.548
I want to be your horn.

37:10.549 --> 37:11.949
Please touch me once.

37:12.150 --> 37:13.860
All right.

37:14.259 --> 37:16.658
Keep going with the band.

37:16.659 --> 37:19.730
You can contact me whenever you need musical advice.

37:20.029 --> 37:22.630
Dong Jin, with that being said,

37:23.969 --> 37:27.540
can you perform at our school festival and kill it?

37:28.239 --> 37:29.299
Just once.

37:30.469 --> 37:33.139
Well... Just keep it to yourself.

37:34.310 --> 37:35.509
I...

37:35.940 --> 37:38.749
"High school students," "a band," "festival."

37:38.750 --> 37:40.949
I hate the combination of the three.

37:41.750 --> 37:43.889
- Why?
- Some high school band boys...

37:44.350 --> 37:46.420
conned him recently.

37:47.819 --> 37:49.830
What kind of punks swindle you?

37:49.929 --> 37:51.028
What do they look like?

37:51.029 --> 37:52.929
I'm going to find them and crush their faces.

37:52.989 --> 37:54.198
Mr. Kang Hyun Yul.

37:54.199 --> 37:56.129
Yes? That's me.

37:56.130 --> 37:57.330
Pick up the phone. It's for you.

37:57.900 --> 37:58.929
Who is it?

37:59.270 --> 38:02.199
Please excuse me for a moment.

38:06.839 --> 38:07.880
Hyun Yul?

38:09.810 --> 38:11.610
Listen up to what I say from now on.

38:12.049 --> 38:15.718
Don't ever let Dong Jin find out who we are. Never.

38:15.719 --> 38:18.250
You must be out of your mind.

38:18.420 --> 38:21.060
You should do anything to charm him right now. What are you talking...

38:25.690 --> 38:28.360
So what's the name of your school again?

38:28.759 --> 38:29.869
It's Baekwang High School.

38:32.000 --> 38:34.699
Baekwang High School?

38:37.369 --> 38:39.369
What's the name of your band?

38:39.670 --> 38:41.609
We're First Lo...

38:41.610 --> 38:44.079
We're First Luck.

38:44.080 --> 38:45.610
- Yes.
- First Luck?

38:45.779 --> 38:47.849
Luck for good luck?

38:47.850 --> 38:50.190
- It's not...
- That's what it is.

38:50.619 --> 38:53.389
Luck is important when you start for the first time.

38:54.389 --> 38:56.730
Dong Jin. I'm so sorry.

38:57.190 --> 38:59.190
Something urgent came up.

38:59.830 --> 39:01.099
So we should go.

39:01.100 --> 39:02.258
I'm sorry.

39:02.259 --> 39:03.630
- Dong Jin.
- I said to get out.

39:04.630 --> 39:06.969
- Hey.
- Okay. I got it.

39:07.799 --> 39:10.369
You conned him.

39:18.610 --> 39:19.948
I should've known better when the name of the band...

39:19.949 --> 39:21.549
was First Love Memory Manipulators.

39:23.020 --> 39:25.119
I could've become a dragon's orb.

39:26.420 --> 39:28.489
I could've become a unicorn's horn.

39:28.960 --> 39:30.730
- It's over for us now.
- It's over for us now.

39:31.560 --> 39:34.499
Well, things happened. Let's just change the name of the band.

39:34.500 --> 39:35.630
- Gosh.
- My goodness.

39:38.600 --> 39:39.969
They say a crisis is an opportunity.

39:40.469 --> 39:43.568
Let's start anew in the new space with the new name.

39:43.569 --> 39:45.440
For goodness' sake.

39:45.670 --> 39:46.779
It's too late.

39:47.009 --> 39:49.909
We already signed up for the festival as The Manipulators.

39:50.610 --> 39:52.149
I believe in your negotiation skills.

39:52.150 --> 39:54.079
What about the T-shirts we made already?

39:54.080 --> 39:55.178
We can start over.

39:55.179 --> 39:57.448
What about the posters and pamphlets with "The Manipulators" on them?

39:57.449 --> 39:58.749
We can make them again too.

39:58.750 --> 40:00.889
We don't have time.

40:01.089 --> 40:03.690
When will we design and make them?

40:04.089 --> 40:05.859
Moreover, it's an exam period for Bal San.

40:05.860 --> 40:07.159
So we can't even ask him for a new design.

40:12.000 --> 40:13.069
We have a capable designer...

40:13.969 --> 40:15.839
called Yoon Chung Ah.

40:19.770 --> 40:21.880
We also have a talented photographer called Choi Se Gyeong.

40:22.239 --> 40:24.480
What about money? Are you going to steal from someone?

40:24.610 --> 40:27.278
I received the tutoring fee in advance.

40:27.279 --> 40:29.989
Did you see that? If you push the wall, it becomes a bridge.

40:30.219 --> 40:31.920
If you fall somewhere, there will be a hidden treasure.

40:32.250 --> 40:34.020
That's what my grandma always said.

40:36.659 --> 40:38.960
Gosh, you have amazing resilience.

40:39.730 --> 40:41.330
So what's the name of the band?

40:42.460 --> 40:45.299
Let us each think of one before the next practice session.

40:45.469 --> 40:47.869
But we should think it through...

40:48.739 --> 40:49.939
and decide by majority vote.

40:49.940 --> 40:52.210
I don't know. Okay. Let's do it.

40:54.380 --> 40:57.480
So who is going to tell the designer and the photographer?

40:59.150 --> 41:02.420
Eun Gyeol can talk to Chung Ah as they're living together.

41:03.489 --> 41:05.019
- As for Se Gyeong...
- Rock-paper-scissors.

41:05.020 --> 41:07.218
- Rock-paper-scissors.
- Rock-paper-scissors.

41:07.219 --> 41:08.989
Yes!

41:16.799 --> 41:18.330
(Alprazolam)

42:03.679 --> 42:05.080
Why are you here at this hour?

42:07.350 --> 42:09.779
I just have something to tell you. So don't say it's a foul.

42:11.290 --> 42:12.649
- Say it.
- First,

42:12.650 --> 42:14.419
you became the photographer for our band. Congratulations.

42:14.420 --> 42:16.419
Second, the name of our band will change. Just know that.

42:16.420 --> 42:17.888
Third, we're going to discuss the theme in the practice room...

42:17.889 --> 42:18.889
this Saturday.

42:18.890 --> 42:20.429
Don't forget and don't be late. I'm done. Bye.

42:25.630 --> 42:26.799
Are you sick?

42:28.199 --> 42:29.270
You look...

42:31.069 --> 42:32.170
pale.

42:33.679 --> 42:36.810
I'm not pale. I'm just fair.

42:37.650 --> 42:38.949
You're narcissistic. Bye.

42:40.219 --> 42:41.279
Hey.

42:45.690 --> 42:47.060
Can you spare me a moment?

42:48.790 --> 42:50.060
Did he...

42:50.460 --> 42:53.529
practice rock-paper-scissors all the time?

42:54.000 --> 42:55.759
He's good at everything.

42:57.330 --> 42:58.369
Darn it.

42:59.699 --> 43:01.199
(The Day)

43:03.100 --> 43:04.440
(The Day)

43:07.139 --> 43:09.509
But we can still be friends.

43:14.179 --> 43:18.290
(The Day)

43:20.319 --> 43:21.988
- Hello.
- Oh, you came.

43:21.989 --> 43:23.318
- Yes.
- The new issue...

43:23.319 --> 43:24.389
of "Slam Dunk" isn't here yet.

43:24.730 --> 43:25.960
I'm not here for that.

43:26.389 --> 43:28.400
Do you have any books on sign language?

43:28.529 --> 43:29.560
Sign language?

43:30.270 --> 43:31.829
Over there. Check the shelves toward the end.

43:31.830 --> 43:33.400
You might find a few books there.

43:33.969 --> 43:34.969
I'll go and check.

43:36.069 --> 43:37.339
Is sign language trending these days?

44:00.159 --> 44:01.600
Where are we going?

44:04.730 --> 44:05.869
Where are we going?

44:06.369 --> 44:07.540
(Namdaemun Liquor Store)

44:10.639 --> 44:12.709
Hey, I get that life is tough.

44:12.710 --> 44:14.080
But you shouldn't drink alcohol or smoke.

44:14.179 --> 44:15.309
What are you talking about?

44:15.310 --> 44:16.440
I'm here to exchange foreign currency.

44:16.880 --> 44:18.880
- Exchange what?
- Come with me.

44:19.750 --> 44:20.750
Hey.

44:26.350 --> 44:29.489
Come on. It's not counterfeit.

44:29.560 --> 44:32.289
If you give me a good rate, I'll only come to your store.

44:32.290 --> 44:34.529
I have a lot of dollars at home.

44:36.560 --> 44:38.069
I'm giving you a good rate because you're pretty.

44:38.270 --> 44:39.330
Thank you.

44:39.929 --> 44:40.940
(Ten-dollar bill)

44:49.009 --> 44:50.750
Queen of Cello, my foot.

44:50.949 --> 44:52.810
You're a pro at this.

44:53.150 --> 44:55.178
Why did you bring me here?

44:55.179 --> 44:56.919
For the minimum safety measure.

44:56.920 --> 44:58.049
Not as your sidekick?

44:58.449 --> 44:59.818
If a young girl walks around streets like this alone...

44:59.819 --> 45:01.318
with wads of money,

45:01.319 --> 45:03.460
as a worst-case scenario, 1 of these 2 things usually happens.

45:03.560 --> 45:05.759
She either gets conned or ends up in danger.

45:06.529 --> 45:08.859
It was a misjudgement on my part to use a guy who can't even curse...

45:08.860 --> 45:10.400
as my bodyguard, though.

45:10.969 --> 45:12.400
What a nice way to thank me...

45:12.699 --> 45:14.400
when I came all the way here for you.

45:15.100 --> 45:17.638
"Hey, I get that life is tough."

45:17.639 --> 45:19.040
"But you shouldn't drink alcohol or smoke."

45:20.040 --> 45:21.309
Are you a boomer?

45:21.310 --> 45:23.379
Besides, when the lady was giving me a bad rate,

45:23.380 --> 45:25.049
you just stood there and said, "Okay."

45:25.480 --> 45:26.549
Are you an idiot?

45:28.250 --> 45:30.520
- I'll learn how to curse.
- Forget it.

45:30.690 --> 45:32.889
Now that I found my go-to lady, I can come here alone next time.

45:33.319 --> 45:34.618
You'll come back here?

45:34.619 --> 45:36.289
I told you. I have a lot of dollars at home.

45:36.290 --> 45:38.028
Where did you get that much cash?

45:38.029 --> 45:40.559
I sold my cello because I'd rather die than play it.

45:40.560 --> 45:42.299
- You too?
- "You too?"

45:43.159 --> 45:44.368
What did you sell?

45:44.369 --> 45:46.229
A guitar. Where did you sell it to?

45:46.230 --> 45:48.299
- At a musical instrument store.
- This can't be.

45:49.100 --> 45:50.440
Is she my helper?

45:50.869 --> 45:52.139
Where was the store?

45:52.339 --> 45:53.609
Was it in front of Hongdae?

45:53.610 --> 45:55.979
No. I sold it in the US.

45:55.980 --> 45:57.809
The store handled classical instruments.

45:57.810 --> 45:59.080
I see.

45:59.580 --> 46:02.049
You should go now. Thanks for coming here with me,

46:02.179 --> 46:03.949
although you weren't much of a help.

46:04.290 --> 46:05.690
Hey, where are you going? You should go home.

46:06.250 --> 46:08.290
Gosh, where are you going?

46:09.290 --> 46:11.259
When I sold the cello, the owner told me...

46:11.360 --> 46:13.960
to go on a trip at least before I died.

46:14.500 --> 46:16.259
It wasn't a bad idea.

46:16.600 --> 46:18.799
There was a place I wanted to go alone.

46:19.029 --> 46:20.670
Happy now? Bye.

46:25.710 --> 46:27.279
(Noodles)

46:31.179 --> 46:32.210
All right.

46:50.100 --> 46:53.400
What do you think about this drawing for your band T-shirts?

46:54.469 --> 46:57.310
Gosh. You've been thinking about our shirts.

46:59.440 --> 47:01.980
You want to put this drawing on our T-shirts?

47:08.319 --> 47:09.779
It's a painting by Frida Kahlo.

47:10.319 --> 47:11.920
She's my favourite painter.

47:14.759 --> 47:15.819
I see.

47:17.159 --> 47:19.860
Why do you like her?

47:22.060 --> 47:23.060
She's strong.

47:24.069 --> 47:25.130
What?

47:28.040 --> 47:29.798
She was beautiful when facing pain.

47:29.799 --> 47:31.409
She was strong to the end.

47:32.170 --> 47:34.709
Life tortured her endlessly.

47:34.710 --> 47:37.150
But she showed life what she was made of with this painting.

47:43.819 --> 47:46.020
With this watermelon painting? How?

47:50.560 --> 47:53.389
Try to find out yourself. It's hidden in the painting.

47:56.730 --> 47:57.770
In the painting?

48:11.380 --> 48:13.449
What could it be?

48:16.650 --> 48:17.690
I see.

48:19.319 --> 48:22.520
"Viva la Vida."

48:25.830 --> 48:26.929
What does this mean?

48:28.759 --> 48:31.069
"Long live life."

48:48.549 --> 48:49.650
The other way around?

48:52.619 --> 48:54.159
I see. Like this? Sorry.

48:57.929 --> 48:59.889
After many years had passed,

49:00.400 --> 49:01.699
my father told me this one day.

49:02.600 --> 49:04.569
Thanks to the saying he learned from Mom,

49:04.730 --> 49:06.699
he was able to endure the hardships of his life.

49:08.440 --> 49:11.110
In happy or painful moments,

49:11.770 --> 49:14.239
he remembered that saying as if it were a song.

49:32.659 --> 49:34.460
The place you wanted to come alone...

49:34.600 --> 49:35.900
was this double feature theatre?

49:37.029 --> 49:38.730
No. Not really.

49:39.469 --> 49:41.440
There aren't any theatres like this where I'm from.

49:41.770 --> 49:42.839
I was just curious.

49:45.639 --> 49:46.969
Stop thinking about that.

49:47.810 --> 49:48.909
About what?

49:49.940 --> 49:51.080
About dying.

49:57.319 --> 49:59.020
Did you really come back to Korea to die?

50:11.369 --> 50:12.469
But you won't die.

50:13.199 --> 50:15.569
You'll be happy with a daughter who's as rebellious as you.

50:15.900 --> 50:18.839
You will age beautifully, gracefully, and elegantly.

50:19.339 --> 50:20.409
On top of that,

50:21.279 --> 50:23.339
you will change the fate of a boy.

50:24.449 --> 50:26.009
How do you know that?

50:26.380 --> 50:28.179
I saw that in the future.

50:34.190 --> 50:35.719
Everyone just goes on with their lives...

50:36.460 --> 50:39.730
while giving meaning to their lives or trying to find meaning.

50:40.259 --> 50:42.199
They do their best to rationalize their lives.

50:44.500 --> 50:46.670
You don't have to try so hard to be impressive.

50:48.069 --> 50:50.810
Continuing to live is already a great feat.

50:53.839 --> 50:55.080
But who knows?

50:56.279 --> 50:57.750
Besides, aren't you a little curious...

50:58.480 --> 51:02.020
about the kind of luck that will come your way in the future...

51:02.750 --> 51:04.650
and how your story will go?

51:07.489 --> 51:08.520
On that note,

51:11.389 --> 51:13.029
you should live until the festival.

51:15.029 --> 51:16.630
Why until the festival?

51:16.799 --> 51:17.830
Because...

51:19.230 --> 51:21.270
I'm going to be really cool at the festival.

51:23.440 --> 51:25.770
Gosh. You're ridiculous.

51:25.869 --> 51:27.610
You're really not shy about tooting your own horn.

51:34.850 --> 51:36.749
He said it out of gratitude when he was happy.

51:36.750 --> 51:38.819
But it became a swear word when he was suffering.

51:58.440 --> 52:00.040
At times, it was like thanking the deity.

52:07.520 --> 52:08.750
I got a fax machine.

52:22.500 --> 52:24.429
At times, it was like chanting a spell to lift a curse.

52:26.529 --> 52:28.469
Viva la Vida!

52:28.670 --> 52:30.069
Let's talk often now.

52:39.449 --> 52:42.650
My father told me with a smile that that's what he said to the world.

52:44.520 --> 52:47.360
"Viva la Vida." Long live life.

52:50.290 --> 52:51.330
- Watermelon?
- Watermelon?

52:52.060 --> 52:53.528
Hey, are you talking about the green fruit...

52:53.529 --> 52:55.000
with red flesh inside?

52:55.259 --> 52:57.868
- Yes.
- No way. You're joking, right?

52:57.869 --> 52:59.529
Never. I'm being serious.

52:59.600 --> 53:00.969
Have you gone mad?

53:01.100 --> 53:03.539
Hey, you want to name our band Watermelon?

53:03.540 --> 53:05.008
All right. Listen up.

53:05.009 --> 53:06.609
Her name is Frida Kahlo.

53:06.610 --> 53:09.778
She was a Mexican painter with a unibrow.

53:09.779 --> 53:12.109
For her last painting, she painted watermelons.

53:12.110 --> 53:15.049
There's a really cool saying on her painting.

53:15.250 --> 53:16.449
Do you know what it is?

53:16.750 --> 53:18.149
"Viva la Vida!"

53:18.150 --> 53:20.118
- Long live life.
- Long live life.

53:20.119 --> 53:22.020
Hey, how did you know?

53:22.819 --> 53:25.629
- I'm totally on board with this.
- Hey.

53:25.630 --> 53:27.859
- You're on board. Nice.
- I'm on board.

53:27.860 --> 53:30.928
Hey, we can go with Viva or La Vida then.

53:30.929 --> 53:32.569
You have to be super lame...

53:32.969 --> 53:34.569
to like a name, Watermelon.

53:34.839 --> 53:36.869
Hey, let's go with our old name then.

53:37.040 --> 53:38.610
I like Watermelon.

53:39.069 --> 53:40.069
Listen.

53:41.080 --> 53:42.080
"Sweetie,"

53:42.710 --> 53:44.448
"why is your band named Watermelon?"

53:44.449 --> 53:45.850
"Well, you see,"

53:46.409 --> 53:49.449
"there was a painter named Frida Kahlo a long time ago."

53:50.080 --> 53:52.619
"She said, 'Long live life.'"

53:53.889 --> 53:55.258
Hey, doesn't it sound really cool?

53:55.259 --> 53:56.589
- That's what I'm talking about.
- Right?

53:57.259 --> 53:58.960
What do you say? Should we go with it?

53:59.360 --> 54:00.658
- Go!
- Go!

54:00.659 --> 54:01.659
Yes!

54:02.199 --> 54:03.230
What about you guys?

54:05.330 --> 54:06.369
Then let's use an English word...

54:07.029 --> 54:08.540
to keep the last ounce of my pride.

54:09.270 --> 54:10.270
I'm embarrassed...

54:11.440 --> 54:13.009
to call our band Watermelon.

54:14.009 --> 54:17.139
"Watermelon?" Hey, that sounds nice.

54:17.949 --> 54:18.949
Are you in?

54:19.210 --> 54:20.879
Sprinkle a lot of sugar then.

54:20.880 --> 54:22.119
So a lot of girls like our band.

54:24.350 --> 54:25.420
Watermelon Sugar?

54:26.449 --> 54:28.560
I like it! Should we go with it?

54:28.960 --> 54:30.020
- Go.
- Go.

54:30.460 --> 54:33.560
Come on. I can barely hear you guys.

54:34.199 --> 54:35.400
Should we go with it?

54:36.730 --> 54:40.699
- Go!
- Go!

54:50.080 --> 54:51.150
- Hey!
- Hey!

54:53.549 --> 54:54.580
- Hey!
- Hey!

54:57.080 --> 54:58.089
- Hey!
- Hey!

55:00.619 --> 55:01.690
- Hey!
- Hey!

55:02.520 --> 55:04.859
What? No way

55:04.860 --> 55:07.159
Is the sun already up?

55:09.460 --> 55:14.299
It's bright outside the window now

55:16.869 --> 55:21.839
There's a spring in my step this morning

55:23.710 --> 55:28.219
As everyone hums

55:31.119 --> 55:34.959
- They're waiting for the sunny day - They're waiting for the sunny day

55:34.960 --> 55:38.459
- With heart-fluttering sensations - With heart-fluttering sensations

55:38.460 --> 55:41.999
- The streets are full of people - The streets are full of people

55:42.000 --> 55:45.469
- Exchanging friendly glances - Exchanging friendly glances

55:46.500 --> 55:47.500
- Hey!
- Hey!

55:50.040 --> 55:51.040
- Hey!
- Hey!

55:53.569 --> 55:54.639
- Hey!
- Hey!

55:57.080 --> 55:58.150
- Hey!
- Hey!

55:59.049 --> 56:01.318
What? No way

56:01.319 --> 56:03.580
Has the night deepened already?

56:06.089 --> 56:10.719
I had no idea time flew by

56:11.290 --> 56:12.460
Hit the high notes.

56:13.330 --> 56:18.330
The white street lamp has turned on

56:20.369 --> 56:24.739
To shine the street after the sun had gone down

56:52.630 --> 56:53.630
What are you doing?

57:14.389 --> 57:15.389
Let's check that.

57:21.759 --> 57:22.759
Oh, no.

57:25.600 --> 57:26.799
Sir!

57:47.790 --> 57:48.819
Hi.

57:50.860 --> 57:51.889
Hi.

57:52.529 --> 57:53.759
Well,

57:54.799 --> 57:59.730
I hope we can work well together from now on.

58:02.000 --> 58:05.110
Actually, I'm not good at sign language.

58:06.069 --> 58:08.779
But I've been learning sign language diligently lately.

58:09.310 --> 58:11.150
I see. I didn't know.

58:11.949 --> 58:12.980
Sorry.

58:16.980 --> 58:17.989
You can do this!

58:21.119 --> 58:22.259
Let's go inside.

58:25.630 --> 58:29.359
- They're waiting for the sunny day - They're waiting for the sunny day

58:29.360 --> 58:32.899
- With heart-fluttering sensations - With heart-fluttering sensations

58:32.900 --> 58:36.368
- The streets are full of people - The streets are full of people

58:36.369 --> 58:40.139
- Exchanging friendly glances - Exchanging friendly glances

58:40.980 --> 58:42.009
- Hey!
- Hey!

58:44.480 --> 58:45.509
- Hey!
- Hey!

58:48.020 --> 58:49.020
- Hey!
- Hey!

58:51.549 --> 58:52.549
- Hey!
- Hey!

58:55.360 --> 58:57.488
Then are any of the other co-members still working...

58:57.489 --> 58:59.428
in the music industry?

58:59.429 --> 59:01.559
- No one. I'm the only one.
- My gosh.

59:01.560 --> 59:02.630
- No one. I'm the only one.
- My gosh.

59:03.299 --> 59:05.469
Unfortunately, we had to disband after a short while...

59:05.630 --> 59:07.630
because one of the members caused big trouble.

59:08.199 --> 59:10.399
Thanks to him, our performance at the festival was ruined.

59:10.400 --> 59:12.109
The band got disbanded.

59:12.110 --> 59:15.310
The only thing I got out of the band was my relationship with Mr. Oh.

59:15.679 --> 59:17.879
If the band got disbanded over the incident,

59:17.880 --> 59:19.580
it must have been quite serious.

59:21.980 --> 59:23.049
It was.

59:23.650 --> 59:27.619
Because of that incident, one of the members got hurt badly.

59:30.460 --> 59:31.829
(Special thanks to Yoon Do Hyun, )

59:31.830 --> 59:33.190
(Park Ho San, Kim Jun Hyung, and Park Han Sol)

01:00:00.219 --> 01:00:05.060
(Twinkling Watermelon)

01:00:05.529 --> 01:00:07.959
Dad's accident will take place tomorrow, the day of the rehearsal.

01:00:07.960 --> 01:00:10.329
Everyone, gather around. The order of the rehearsal came out.

01:00:10.330 --> 01:00:11.928
It's tomorrow at 3pm.

01:00:11.929 --> 01:00:13.798
What's his deal?

01:00:13.799 --> 01:00:15.638
Okay. I'll help you.

01:00:15.639 --> 01:00:17.669
What's going to happen tomorrow?

01:00:17.670 --> 01:00:20.039
Who's going to cause the accident? Please tell me!

01:00:20.040 --> 01:00:22.008
You've been manipulating me through Se Gyeong?

01:00:22.009 --> 01:00:24.778
Why are you taking it this far?

01:00:24.779 --> 01:00:26.809
I pleaded with you, but you wouldn't listen.

01:00:26.810 --> 01:00:28.318
I know your future.

01:00:28.319 --> 01:00:30.579
I found out how to change your life.

01:00:30.580 --> 01:00:32.789
I'll now show you the consequences...

01:00:32.790 --> 01:00:34.119
of stabbing me in the back.
